nalysis tool, not presented as a text-bio generative model.","evidence_snippet":"\"a pre-trained transformer model (scGPT) was fine-tuned using an integrated dataset\" for transcriptomic analysis"},{"record_id":"rec_002508","paper_type":"application_wrapper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"LLOKI is an integration framework for spatial transcriptomics that uses scGPT to generate unified features and refine embeddings. The text-like model is used as a component inside a downstream wrapper.","evidence_snippet":"\"enable single-cell foundation models such as scGPT to generate unified features\" and \"Batch alignment then refines scGPT-transformed embeddings\""},{"record_id":"rec_002509","paper_type":"benchmark_resource","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"benchmark_resource","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is an evaluation paper focused on zero-shot performance of existing single-cell foundation models. It does not propose a new candidate model.","evidence_snippet":"\"Foundation models such as scGPT and Geneformer have not been rigorously evaluated\" and \"Our evaluation of the zero-shot performance\""},{"record_id":"rec_002510","paper_type":"application_wrapper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The work adapts DeepCDR by using pretrained scGPT cell representations for drug response prediction. This is a downstream application of an existing model, not a new text-bio model.","evidence_snippet":"\"We adapt this framework by leveraging scGPT to generate enriched cell representations\" for drug response prediction"},{"record_id":"rec_002511","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract presents a new model, tGPT, that learns from large-scale transcriptomes using generative pretraining. It explicitly describes autoregressive token-style modeling over gene rankings.","evidence_snippet":"\"we present an approach entitled tGPT\" and \"autoregressively models the ranking of a gene\" as a \"generative pretraining task\""},{"record_id":"rec_002512","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a new predictive framework for genetic perturbation effects, but the abstract does not describe any substantive text or language component. It is a bio ML model rather than a text-bio model.","evidence_snippet":"\"We present GARM (Gradient Aligned Regression with Multi-decoder)\" for predicting transcriptional effects of genetic perturbations"}]}
