36","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract says 'This review explores applications' of multimodal AI for breast cancer detection. Text is mentioned as one modality, but the paper is a review rather than a primary model paper.","evidence_snippet":"\"This review explores applications\" and mentions multimodal medical data including imaging, text, genetic data, and physiological signals"},{"record_id":"rec_002437","paper_type":"benchmark_resource","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"benchmark_resource","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract centers on the Human Phenotype Project as a large-scale prospective cohort and data platform. The foundation model is secondary to the cohort/resource contribution, and no text component is described.","evidence_snippet":"\"The Human Phenotype Project (HPP) is a large-scale deep-phenotype prospective cohort\" and \"we present a multi-modal foundation AI model\""},{"record_id":"rec_002438","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract frames the paper as an article that 'examines' AI-enhanced risk prediction approaches. It is a general review of methods, not a primary text-bio model.","evidence_snippet":"\"This article examines how AI-enhanced approaches revolutionize health data collection and predictive modeling\""},{"record_id":"rec_002439","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a primary multimodal cancer model using gene expression, clinical records, and tissue images. The abstract does not describe a substantive text/language component.","evidence_snippet":"\"The research presents a robust hybrid machine learning-based approach\" using gene expression, clinical record, and tissue images"},{"record_id":"rec_002440","paper_type":"application_wrapper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract proposes an application framework combining FL, GANs, blockchain, and explainability for medical AI deployment. This is a system wrapper around existing methods, not a substantive text-bio model.","evidence_snippet":"\"A novel 6G-enabled Federated Learning-Generative Adversarial Network (FL-GAN) framework is proposed\" with EHRs, images, and genomic profiles"}]}
