tificial intelligence\"; discusses existing AI applications and programs"},{"record_id":"rec_001204","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is an editorial/commentary on genomic language models, not a primary model paper. It discusses gLMs as tools to decode DNA sequences and frames their medical potential.","evidence_snippet":"\"This article examines the emergence of gLMs\"; \"gLMs... decode DNA sequences\""},{"record_id":"rec_001205","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"Introduces GC-MERGE for predicting gene expression from genomic and histone-modification data. No text/language component is described in the abstract.","evidence_snippet":"\"predict gene expression\"; \"integrates measurements of ... histone modifications\""},{"record_id":"rec_001206","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"unclear","text_bio_bridge_present":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"text_component_unclear","decision_rationale":"This is a review of diffusion models and their applications in bioinformatics, not an original model paper. The abstract lists bioinformatics domains covered by the review.","evidence_snippet":"\"This review aims to provide a rather thorough overview of the applications of diffusion models in bioinformatics\""},{"record_id":"rec_001207","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"unclear","text_bio_bridge_present":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"text_component_unclear","decision_rationale":"The abstract describes a meta-synthesis/framework paper on AI-driven healthcare innovation rather than a primary generative text-bio model. It summarizes prior studies across multi-omics and clinical AI use cases.","evidence_snippet":"\"This qualitative-quantitative meta-synthesis\"; \"integrates generative AI, deep learning, and multi-modal data\""},{"record_id":"rec_001208","paper_type":"application_wrapper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a multi-stage workflow that uses external LLMs and a vision-language foundation model to generate and score prompts against histopathology tiles. The text-bio link is operational, but the paper is a wrapper around existing models.","evidence_snippet":"\"generates... natural-language prompts\"; \"Each approved prompt... is scored using the vision language foundation model (CONCH)\""}]}
