003804","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract says the work is a systematic review and also notes it compiled a catalogue of public PitNET omics resources. That makes it a review/resource paper, not a primary model paper.","evidence_snippet":"\"This systematic review aimed to evaluate\"; \"compiled a comprehensive catalogue of all publicly available PitNET omics resources\""},{"record_id":"rec_003805","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"paper_type_unclear","decision_rationale":"The title frames this as an application-focused article on AI/ML in cell and gene therapy, and the abstract fragment mentions foundation models and generative AI only in a broad discussion. It does not support a substantive new text-bio model.","evidence_snippet":"\"Advancing cell and gene therapy: Application of AI/ML in clinical development and patient management\"; \"large foundation models such as GPT-5\""},{"record_id":"rec_003806","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract points to a generative modeling paper on protein localization and single-cell biology. No text/language component is described in the record.","evidence_snippet":"\"identity-preserving latent diffusion\"; \"protein localization\"; \"single-cell resolution\""},{"record_id":"rec_003807","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"paper_type_unclear","decision_rationale":"The title is a broad thematic overview of AI-powered nanomedicine, and the abstract fragment mentions GPT in passing rather than a new text-bio model. The record reads like a review or perspective.","evidence_snippet":"\"Artificial intelligence-powered nanomedicine\"; \"such as generative pre-trained transformers (GPT)\""},{"record_id":"rec_003808","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"no","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC1_no_bio_modality","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The title and abstract center on cognition and embedding-space navigation, with biology appearing only as a distant analogy. There is no clear biological modality or text-bio model described.","evidence_snippet":"\"remapping and navigation of an embedding space\"; \"generative models in AI\""}]}
./data/screening_codex_full_2026-07-06/role_logs/adjudicator/batch_0204.stderr.log:1617:./data/screening_codex_full_2026-07-06/role_logs/architecture_reviewer/batch_0056.stderr.log:1046:./data/screening_codex_full_2026-07-06/role_logs/scope_reviewer/batch_0169.stderr.log:108:{"results":[{"record_id":"rec_001345","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"Primary computational framework over MERFISH/scRNA-seq spatial transcriptomics. No substantive text or language component is described.","evidence_snippet":"“multimodal single-cell and spatial transcriptomics with generative AI” and “deep learning” for scRNA and MERFISH"},{"record_id":"rec_001346","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a deep learning prognosis model using images, clinical records, and genomic data. The abstract does not describe any text/language component.","evidence_snippet":"“medical images, clinical records, and genomic information” with CNNs, RNNs, and fully connected layers"},{"record_id":"rec_001347","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"Primary biology research on a single-cell spatiotemporal transcriptomic atlas and organoid modeling. No text or language-model component is evident.","evidence_snippet":"“single-cell spatiotemporal transcriptomic atlas” and “human DRG organoids”"},{"record_id":"rec_001348","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract is a review/editorial on pathology foundation models rather than a primary model report. It explicitly discusses visual-language models integrating pathology images and biomedical text.","evidence_snippet":"“Foundation models are revolutionising pathology” and “visual-language models ... integrate histopathological images with biomedical text”"},{"record_id":"rec_001349","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is explicitly a systematic review of machine learning for type 2 diabetes prediction. The abstract centers on clinical, EHR, and omics data, not text.","evidence_snippet":"“A Systematic Review” and “clinical measures, electronic health records, genomic and proteomic profiles”"},{"record_id":"rec_001350","paper_type":"application_wrapper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The LLM is used on curated multi-omics signatures encoded as structured text prompts for subtype classification. That is a wrapper-style application, not a substantive text-bio foundational model.","evidence_snippet":"“fine-tuned Large Language Models (LLMs)” on “multi-omics signatures and clinical metadata encoded as structured text prompts”"},{"record_id":"rec_001351","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a primary foundation-model paper for DNA with explicit language-model-style pretraining. The abstract describes bidirectional autoregressive and masked modeling over biological sequences.","evidence_snippet":"“first bidirectional DNA foundation model” and “combines the optimization efficiency of autoregressive modeling with the bidirectional comprehension of masked modeling”"},{"record_id":"rec_001352","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract introduces Med-PaLM M as a large multimodal generative model spanning clinical language, imaging, and genomics. Although it also presents a benchmark, the model is a central primary contribution.","evidence_snippet":"“We then introduce Med-PaLM Multimodal (Med-PaLM M)” and “clinical language, imaging, and genomics”"}]}
./data/screening_codex_full_2026-07-06/role_logs/adjudicator/batch_0204.stderr.log:1624:./data/screening_codex_full_2026-07-06/role_logs/architecture_reviewer/batch_0056.stderr.log:1069:./data/screening_codex_full_2026-07-06/role_logs/scope_reviewer/batch_0222.stdout.log:1:{"results":[{"record_id":"rec_001769","paper_type":"benchmark_resource","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"benchmark_resource","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a platform/resource paper that harmonizes biomedical databases into a unified knowledge graph and TNG structure. The abstract emphasizes the resource and data structure rather than a new model.","evidence_snippet":"“all-in-one platform” ... “integrating 11 entity types and 30 relation types from 43 databases” and “novel Textual-Numeric Graph (TNG) data-structure”"},{"record_id":"rec_001770","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The title and abstract describe a narrative review of biomarkers and predictive models for rectal cancer response. No new candidate model is presented.","evidence_snippet":"“This narrative review synthesizes recent progress” and “By synthesizing the existing evidence, this review”"},{"record_id":"rec_001771","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a primary model paper for RNA language modeling with adaptive tokenization. The model is trained on RNA sequences and explicitly uses language-model style tokenization and next-token objectives.","evidence_snippet":"“BiRNA-BERT ... trained on 36 million non-coding RNA sequences” and “RNA language modeling with adaptive tokenization”"},{"record_id":"rec_001772","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract describes a self-supervised pathomics transformer on whole-slide images for immunotherapy outcome prediction. It includes biological interpretation from scRNA-seq, but no substantive text/language component.","evidence_snippet":"“H&E-stained slides from pan-cancer patients were digitized as whole slide images” and “single-cell RNA sequencing analyses were performed”"},{"record_id":"rec_001773","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a primary genomic foundation model paper with next-token pretraining and cross-modal task tokens. The abstract explicitly includes DNA-to-text functional descriptions.","evidence_snippet":"“Omni-DNA, a family of cross-modal multi-task models” and “DNA sequences to textual functional descriptions”"},{"record_id":"rec_001774","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"text_bio_bridge_unclear","decision_rationale":"Mamba is presented as a general sequence model and is evaluated on language and genomics. The abstract does not clearly describe a substantive text-bio bridge or cross-modal integration mechanism.","evidence_snippet":"“achieves state-of-the-art performance across several modalities such as language, audio, and genomics”"},{"record_id":"rec_001775","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a narrative review of ADR prediction using EHRs and multimodal models. It synthesizes prior work rather than presenting a new model.","evidence_snippet":"“This narrative review synthesizes recent progress” and “development and validation of predictive models that leverage EHRs”"},{"record_id":"rec_001776","paper_type":"benchmark_resource","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"benchmark_resource","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract is primarily a project/resource description about harmonizing plant metabarcoding pipelines, databases, and best practices. It also proposes multimodal modeling, but the dominant contribution is resource and pipeline infrastructure.","evidence_snippet":"“best practice recommendations, optimizing analysis pipelines, and creating user-friendly reference databases” and “train a large language model (LLM) on relevant scientific literature”"}]}
./data/screening_codex_full_2026-07-06/role_logs/adjudicator/batch_0204.stderr.log:1627:./data/screening_codex_full_2026-07-06/role_logs/architecture_reviewer/batch_0056.stderr.log:1082:./data/screening_codex_full_2026-07-06/role_logs/scope_reviewer/batch_0068.stdout.log:1:{"results":[{"record_id":"rec_000537","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"Primary model paper using tumor transcriptomes and a developmental MLP classifier. No substantive text/language component is described.","evidence_snippet":"“map the single-cell organogenesis... to the transcriptomes of over 10,000 tumors” and “construct a developmental multilayer perceptron classifier”"},{"record_id":"rec_000538","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"Primary computational model for RNA-protein interaction prediction based on CLIP-seq data and graph neural networks. The abstract does not indicate any text/language component.","evidence_snippet":"“construct a de novo predictor of RNA-protein interactions based on graph neural networks”"},{"record_id":"rec_000539","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"Primary multimodal deep-learning study combining pathology images and molecular profile data. It is not a text-bio model and no language component is described.","evidence_snippet":"“jointly examine pathology whole-slide images and molecular profile data”"},{"record_id":"rec_000540","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"Primary prediction model for MSI status using H&E images and molecular data. The abstract provides no evidence of a substantive text component.","evidence_snippet":"“predict MSI status based solely on hematoxylin and eosin images” and “integrating H&E image with molecular data”"},{"record_id":"rec_000541","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is explicitly a review of 43 studies on multimodal cancer prognosis models, not a primary candidate model paper.","evidence_snippet":"“In this review, we have gathered 43 state-of-the-art scientific papers”"},{"record_id":"rec_000542","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"Primary single-cell analysis using paired CSF and blood transcriptomic data with supervised deep learning. No substantive text/language component is described.","evidence_snippet":"“single-cell analyses of paired cerebrospinal fluid and peripheral blood” and “supervised deep learning of single-cell transcriptomes”"},{"record_id":"rec_000543","paper_type":"benchmark_resource","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"benchmark_resource","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The paper presents a web database/resource for motif analyses and access to prediction results, rather than a primary candidate model paper. No text component is evident.","evidence_snippet":"“DESSO-DB: A web database” and “provides motif prediction results and visualizations”"},{"record_id":"rec_000544","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a review article on deep learning in genomics, not a primary model paper. The abstract discusses applications and future possibilities rather than a specific text-bio model.","evidence_snippet":"“We review here the new applications that the use of deep learning enables in the field”"}]}
./data/screening_codex_full_2026-07-06/role_logs/adjudicator/batch_0204.stderr.log:1628:./data/screening_codex_full_2026-07-06/role_logs/architecture_reviewer/batch_0056.stderr.log:1089:./data/screening_codex_full_2026-07-06/role_logs/scope_reviewer/batch_0281.response.txt:1:{"results":[{"record_id":"rec_002241","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"A primary comparison of LSTM and BERT on viral genomic sequences. The abstract describes genomic classification, not a substantive text or generative text-bio bridge.","evidence_snippet":"“classifying genomic sequences of HIV and SARS-CoV-2” and “BERT-based transformers”"},{"record_id":"rec_002242","paper_type":"application_wrapper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This uses the previously described DeepTCR framework and modifies its featurization for prediction. It is an applied downstream use on TCR/HLA data rather than a new candidate text-bio model.","evidence_snippet":"“We employ DeepTCR, a previously described set of deep learning algorithms” and “modified the DeepTCR Featurization block”"},{"record_id":"rec_002243","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract explicitly presents a foundational model transferring linguistic capabilities from English to DNA sequences. It also maps DNA words to English equivalents and fine-tunes with English segmentation data.","evidence_snippet":"“trained a foundational model capable of transferring linguistic capabilities from English to DNA sequences”"},{"record_id":"rec_002244","paper_type":"application_wrapper","bio_modality_present":"no","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a bibliometric/topic-modeling study over PubMed titles and abstracts, not a primary bio-text foundation model. The biological dataset is synthetic and illustrative rather than the candidate model’s core modality.","evidence_snippet":"“treats PubMed titles and abstracts as data” and “generated a fully synthetic neuroimmune salivary dataset”"},{"record_id":"rec_002245","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The model is a cfDNA whole-genome sequencing classifier built from fragment and coverage features. No substantive text or language component is described.","evidence_snippet":"“integrating fragment end motif by size (FEMS) with genomic coverage (COV) of cfDNA”"},{"record_id":"rec_002246","paper_type":"application_wrapper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract presents a platform that mines biomedical text and triangulates it with single-cell RNA-seq insights. That is a text-to-biology application layer rather than a new foundational model.","evidence_snippet":"“dynamic inference from ... unstructured biomedical text” and “triangulation with Single Cell RNA-sequencing based insights”"},{"record_id":"rec_002247","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a DNA enhancer prediction model using CNN/LSTM with k-mer and DNAshape features. The NLP wording is methodological, but no substantive text-bio model is described.","evidence_snippet":"“using natural language processing, convolutional neural network, and long short-term memory to predict the enhancer elements”"},{"record_id":"rec_002248","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract describes a novel LLM-based model trained on MTB genomic data to predict antibiotic resistance. It directly bridges transformer language modeling with a biological prediction task.","evidence_snippet":"“leveraging large language models to predict antibiotic resistance in Mycobacterium tuberculosis” and “trained and evaluated on genomic data”"}]}
./data/screening_codex_full_2026-07-06/role_logs/adjudicator/batch_0204.stderr.log:1632:./data/screening_codex_full_2026-07-06/role_logs/architecture_reviewer/batch_0056.stderr.log:1133:{"results":[{"record_id":"rec_000441","paper_type":"review_editorial","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract says this is a review of AI applications in PET imaging, not a primary model. It discusses imaging tasks and future directions, but no generative or foundation model is presented.","evidence_snippet":"\"This review aims to take a journey into the transformative impact of artificial intelligence (AI) on positron emission tomography (PET) imaging.\""},{"record_id":"rec_000442","paper_type":"review_editorial","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract is a systematic survey of deep learning in genomics and histopathology, so it is not a candidate model paper. It summarizes applications rather than describing a generative or foundation model.","evidence_snippet":"\"we present a systematic survey of the academic literature\""},{"record_id":"rec_000443","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract presents a prognostic prediction model for ovarian cancer survival using multi-omics inputs. It is a predictive system, with no generative mechanism or foundation-model evidence.","evidence_snippet":"\"we propose a deep learning model... superior ... in predicting ovarian cancer prognosis\""},{"record_id":"rec_000444","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"yes","foundation_model_evidence":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"foundation_model_evidence_unclear","decision_rationale":"The abstract explicitly calls inClust+ a deep generative framework and describes encoder/decoder-based cross-modal generation. It does not clearly show foundation-model-like broad pretraining or transferable pretraining.","evidence_snippet":"\"a deep generative framework\" and \"output-mask module behind the decoder\""},{"record_id":"rec_000445","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"MIDAS is described as a deep probabilistic framework for integration, imputation, and batch correction, with no explicit generative mechanism. It does show self-supervised alignment, transfer learning, and knowledge transfer to new data.","evidence_snippet":"\"self-supervised modality alignment\" and \"flexible and accurate knowledge transfer from the atlas to new data\""},{"record_id":"rec_000446","paper_type":"review_editorial","generative_model_present":"unclear","foundation_model_evidence":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"mixed_signals","decision_rationale":"The abstract is a review of LLM components and applications in bioinformatics, not a candidate model paper. It mentions foundation models and pretraining, but only in обзор/summary form.","evidence_snippet":"\"we will provide a comprehensive overview of the essential components of large language models (LLMs) in bioinformatics\""},{"record_id":"rec_000447","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"Microsnoop is a self-supervised representation tool trained on large-scale microscopy images and described as a generalist tool. That supports foundation-like breadth, but it is not generative.","evidence_snippet":"\"trained on large-scale microscopy images using masked self-supervised learning\" and \"generalist tool\""},{"record_id":"rec_000448","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"TFTF is a predictive TFBS detection model. The abstract describes multimodal language architecture for detection, not a generative model or foundation-style pretraining.","evidence_snippet":"\"first approach to accurately perform genome-wide detection\" and \"Users can train TFTF model and discover TFBS with their own data\""}]}
./data/screening_codex_full_2026-07-06/role_logs/adjudicator/batch_0204.stderr.log:1652:{"results":[{"record_id":"rec_003758","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"unclear","generative_model_present":"yes","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"text_bio_bridge_unclear","decision_rationale":"The title/abstract read as a review of machine-guided synthetic biology part design, and the abstract only mentions generative models such as GPT in background context. It does not clearly present a new primary text-bio foundation model.","evidence_snippet":"\"Machine-Guided Approaches for Synthetic Biology Part Design\"; \"models like Generative Pretrained Transformer (GPT)\""},{"record_id":"rec_003763","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"unclear","text_component_present":"unclear","text_bio_bridge_present":"unclear","generative_model_present":"unclear","foundation_model_evidence":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"mixed_signals","decision_rationale":"The title frames sTabNet as a new model, but the abstract fragment is truncated and mixes tabular-data framing with GPT/BERT and single-cell wording. That is not enough to resolve whether it is a generative text-bio foundational model.","evidence_snippet":"\"We introduce sTabNet, a meta-generative framework\"; \"foundational neural network alternative for tabular data\"; \"Single-cell technologies have profoundly advanced our\""},{"record_id":"rec_003766","paper_type":"application_wrapper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a case report, and the only AI use is ChatGPT for language improvement. The biological content is single-cell RNA sequencing, not a text-bio model.","evidence_snippet":"\"used Chat GPT 5.0 in order to improve language\"; \"performed single-cell RNA sequencing (scRNAseq)\""},{"record_id":"rec_003769","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"unclear","generative_model_present":"yes","foundation_model_evidence":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"foundation_model_evidence_unclear","decision_rationale":"The title is explicitly a review, and the abstract only uses GPT-style transformers as examples in medical research. It does not clearly describe a candidate foundation model.","evidence_snippet":"\"A Review of Transformers in Medical Research and Health Care\"; \"Decoder-only models, exemplified by GPT\""},{"record_id":"rec_003770","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"unclear","text_bio_bridge_present":"unclear","generative_model_present":"unclear","foundation_model_evidence":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"text_component_unclear","decision_rationale":"The fragment points to single-cell biology and mentions language-model baselines, but it does not clearly identify the candidate model or its text pathway. The text-bio bridge remains unresolved.","evidence_snippet":"\"Modern single-cell biology\"; \"language model baselines (o3-mini and GPT-4o)\""},{"record_id":"rec_003774","paper_type":"application_wrapper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"HistoGWAS is presented as a downstream histology GWAS framework that leverages foundation and generative models for analysis and interpretation. That reads as an application framework rather than a new generative text-bio foundation model.","evidence_snippet":"\"framework for genome-wide association studies of histology data\"; \"leverages foundation models\"; \"generative models for variant effect interpretation\""}]}
