fer learning\""}]}
./data/screening_codex_full_2026-07-06/role_logs/adjudicator/batch_0103.stdout.log:1:{"results":[{"record_id":"rec_002081","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","generative_model_present":"unclear","foundation_model_evidence":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract explicitly says this is a comprehensive review of AI-driven drug discovery, not a primary model paper. It mentions generative models only as surveyed methods, not as a text-bio foundation model in the record.","evidence_snippet":"\"This paper presents a comprehensive review of recent advancements in AI-driven drug discovery\""},{"record_id":"rec_002083","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"foundation_model_evidence_unclear","decision_rationale":"The paper studies sparse autoencoders on biological embeddings and pretrained single-cell models, but the abstract does not show a substantive text component. The text-only LLM mention is prior motivation, not a text-bio bridge in this paper.","evidence_snippet":"\"explores the potential of SAEs for decomposing embeddings in complex and high-dimensional biological data\""},{"record_id":"rec_002086","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","generative_model_present":"unclear","foundation_model_evidence":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a systematic review of GANs in medicine, so it is not a primary model paper. The abstract summarizes prior synthetic data generation studies rather than presenting a new generative text-bio model.","evidence_snippet":"\"This review examines the landscape of GAN-based synthetic data generation in healthcare\""},{"record_id":"rec_002087","paper_type":"benchmark_resource","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"benchmark_resource","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract says it introduces benchmark datasets and compares model architectures for genomic tasks. That makes it a benchmark/resource paper rather than a new generative text-bio model.","evidence_snippet":"\"introduce a collection of benchmark datasets\" and \"compare the performance of several model architectures\""},{"record_id":"rec_002093","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","generative_model_present":"unclear","foundation_model_evidence":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The record is explicitly a review of LLMs/Transformer-based models for metabolite annotation, not a primary model paper. It discusses applications and future perspectives rather than a new generative architecture.","evidence_snippet":"\"Review\" and \"This review highlights the application and future perspectives\""},{"record_id":"rec_002096","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract presents a multimodal deep belief network for cancer classification using biomedical and imaging data, but no substantive text component is described. The conflict with the architecture reviewer is resolved by the clear absence of text.","evidence_snippet":"\"Multimodal Deep Belief Network\" for \"cancer classification\" and \"including genomic, proteomic, and clinical information\""}]}
./data/screening_codex_full_2026-07-06/role_logs/adjudicator/batch_0213.response.txt:1:{"results":[{"record_id":"rec_003875","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","generative_model_present":"unclear","foundation_model_evidence":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The title and abstract read as a broad overview of plant multi-omics and cite existing models like Spatial Scope, not a new model paper. No substantive text component or text-bio bridge is described.","evidence_snippet":"\"Artificial Intelligence-Enabled Single-Cell Resolution and Spatial Plant Multi-omics\"; \"Models like Spatial Scope\""},{"record_id":"rec_003881","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"unclear","text_bio_bridge_present":"unclear","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"mixed_signals","decision_rationale":"This is a contrastive-learning method for scRNA-seq clustering, which is predictive rather than generative. The mention of natural language data is too thin to establish a substantive text-bio generative model.","evidence_snippet":"\"SEAL: Semantic-Aware Contrastive Learning for scRNA-seq clustering\"; \"image or natural language data\""},{"record_id":"rec_003882","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","generative_model_present":"unclear","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The title explicitly calls it a survey, so this is not a primary model paper. The abstract discusses flow matching as a generative paradigm across biology and life science, not a candidate foundation model.","evidence_snippet":"\"a survey\"; \"powerful paradigm for generative modeling\""},{"record_id":"rec_003883","paper_type":"application_wrapper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"mixed_signals","decision_rationale":"ProTCR uses the pretrained protein language model ProtT5 as a component in a downstream TCR-antigen prediction framework. The abstract supports a wrapper-style application, not a new generative text-bio foundation model.","evidence_snippet":"\"integrates the protein language model ProtT5 with deep learning methods\""},{"record_id":"rec_003885","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","generative_model_present":"unclear","foundation_model_evidence":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"mixed_signals","decision_rationale":"The title reads as a review on AI for lipid nanoparticle design. The abstract fragment only adds a generic BERT-like pretraining analogy, which is insufficient to establish a primary text-bio model.","evidence_snippet":"\"Artificial Intelligence In The Rational Design Of Lipid Nanoparticles For mRNA Therapeutics\"; \"pretraining paradigm (analogous to BERT)\""},{"record_id":"rec_003887","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"mixed_signals","decision_rationale":"The record is about spatial transcriptomics with heterogeneous graph neural networks; the stray mention of natural-language prompts is too fragmentary to establish a real text component or text-bio bridge. No generative or foundation-model evidence is shown.","evidence_snippet":"\"Causal Discovery in Spatially-Resolved Transcriptomics via Heterogeneous Graph Neural Networks\"; \"natural language prompts\""}]}
./data/screening_codex_full_2026-07-06/role_logs/adjudicator/batch_0042.stdout.log:1:{"results":[{"record_id":"rec_000882","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","generative_model_present":"yes","foundation_model_evidence":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"foundation_model_evidence_unclear","decision_rationale":"The abstract describes a generative transformer model for synthetic bacteriophage genomes and compares generated sequences to natural genomes. It does not clearly establish broad foundation-model pretraining.","evidence_snippet":"“the first publicly available generative model for creating synthetic viral genomes”"},{"record_id":"rec_000884","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a deep learning method for detecting RiPP precursors from metagenomes, with no substantive text or language component described. The abstract does not support a generative model.","evidence_snippet":"“developed TrRiPP to identify RiPPs from ocean metagenomes”"},{"record_id":"rec_000885","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The model fuses CT image features with gene features for survival prediction and does not describe any text or language component. It is a supervised predictive architecture, not a generative text-bio model.","evidence_snippet":"“three modules: an image feature extraction module ... a gene feature extraction module ... and an attention fusion network”"},{"record_id":"rec_000887","paper_type":"application_wrapper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a downstream extraction pipeline that combines rules with pretrained NLP models for genomic report processing. The abstract supports wrapper-style use of existing models, not a generative foundation model.","evidence_snippet":"“a hybrid approach of combining rules and pretrained NLP models to extract gene variants”"},{"record_id":"rec_000888","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"foundation_model_evidence_unclear","decision_rationale":"MIXBend uses a pretrained language model (DNABERT) plus physicochemical features to forecast DNA bendability, but the abstract describes prediction rather than generation. Foundation-model breadth is not clearly established.","evidence_snippet":"“a pre-trained language model DNABERT ... are utilized” and “to forecast the DNA bendability”"},{"record_id":"rec_000889","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","generative_model_present":"unclear","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_substantive_text_bio_bridge","uncertainty_reason":"generative_status_unclear","decision_rationale":"The paper trains a genomic language model on millions of metagenomic scaffolds and reports unsupervised corpus learning. The abstract does not show a substantive text-bio bridge, and generation is not stated explicitly.","evidence_snippet":"“trained a genomic language model (gLM) on millions of metagenomic scaffolds”"}]}
