odels with billions of parameters\" and \"multi-task transfer learning\" with new SOTA on property prediction benchmarks"},{"record_id":"rec_003897","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"unclear","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"mixed_signals","decision_rationale":"The title and abstract read like a general discussion of AI for genotoxicity assessment rather than a new model paper. It mentions NLP and an AI model, but no clear generative or foundation-model architecture.","evidence_snippet":"“Natural language processing offers a powerful tool” and “the future of genotoxicity assessment”"},{"record_id":"rec_003899","paper_type":"benchmark_resource","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"benchmark_resource","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The title explicitly says it is evaluating vision foundation models for microscopy classification, so this is a benchmark/evaluation paper. It does not present a generative text-bio model.","evidence_snippet":"“Evaluating Vision Foundation Models for Pixel and Object Classification in Microscopy”"},{"record_id":"rec_003900","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"unclear","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The venue and abstract indicate a review of computational approaches and future directions, not an original generative model. The mention of multimodal foundation models is prospective rather than evidence of a new model.","evidence_snippet":"“Nature Reviews …” and “the generation of multimodal foundation models will leverage”"}]}
