mponent_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","generative_model_present":"yes","foundation_model_evidence":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"foundation_model_evidence_unclear","decision_rationale":"SpatialTopic is a spatial topic model for multiplexed tissue imaging, so it is a primary model paper with a generative architecture. The abstract shows scalability, but not clear foundation-model-style pretraining or reuse.","evidence_snippet":"“a spatial topic model” and “topic modelling framework, originally developed for natural language processing”"},{"record_id":"rec_001608","paper_type":"application_wrapper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a diagnostic application built with standard deep-learning backbones for liver cancer detection. It does not describe a generative text-bio model.","evidence_snippet":"“a deep learning-based diagnosis system” using “CNN, VGG 16, VGG 19, and Inception V3”"},{"record_id":"rec_001609","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","generative_model_present":"unclear","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"generative_status_unclear","decision_rationale":"DNACSE explicitly fine-tunes a DNA language foundation model for DNA barcode identification, so the text-bio bridge and foundation-model evidence are clear. The abstract does not state a clearly generative architecture, so that criterion remains unclear.","evidence_snippet":"“fine-tune the DNA language foundation model”; “DNA barcode identification”"}]}

