or the specific task. Specifically, we learn the optimal kernel size and dilation rate for each convolutional layer in the CNN using the DASH (Diversetask Architecture Search) algorithm [30], which has demonstrated state-of-the-art performance among AutoML methods on the DeepSEA dataset. [truncated]","original_chars":2065},{"section_type":"data_representation","heading":"Methods","heading_level":3,"line_start":33,"line_end":126,"text":"#### Cross-modal fine-tuning\n\nFine-tuning has been a highly effective technique for adapting pre-trained language models to various downstream tasks. However, most existing research focuses on in-modal adaptation, where the finetuning data originates from the same modality as the pre-training data but is tailored for a more specialized focus, such as sentiment analysis or text classification. In such cases, the model operates on the same type of input it was originally trained on. In contrast, cross-modal fi ne-tuning adapts a pre-trained model to work with data from an unseen modalities, such as using text-pre-trained LLMs to address biological questions. Fig. 1A illustrates the distinction between in-modal and cross-modal fine-tuning strategies for genomic tasks.\n\nCross-modal fine-tuning is more challenging than the in-modal fine-tuning due to the modality gap between the pre-training and target task data [14]. Bridge this gap often requires additional data alignment. For instance, to repurpose a pre-trained BERT model for predicting physicochemical and biomedical properties of protein sequences, Vinod et al. [10] introduced R2DL (Representation Reprogramming via Dictionary Learning), a token-level alignment method that learns a sparse linear mapping between English vocabulary embeddings and amino acid embeddings.\n\nRecently, Shen et al [12] proposed a more general distributional alignment technique, ORCA, that adapts various pre-trained transformer models to diverse non-text, non-vision inputs. [truncated]","original_chars":15685}],"docling_markdown":"data/docling_include_no_vlm_2026-07-09/markdown/full_2026_07_06_rec_000323.md","first_pass_outputs":{"scope_reviewer":{"record_id":"full_2026-07-06__rec_000323","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The record presents a new model, L2G, for genomics rather than a review or wrapper. It explicitly combines a pre-trained language model with DNA inputs and aligns language and DNA embeddings.","evidence_snippet":"\"adapts a pre-trained LLM architecture for genomics\"; \"transformer layers from a pre-trained language model\"; \"minimizes the modality gap between DNA embeddings and language embeddings\"; \"cross-modal transfer in genomics\"; \"L2G, a new method\"; \"genomics tasks\"; \"DNA sequence data\"; \"language embeddings\"; \"DNA embeddings\"; \"alignments between different modalities\"; \"task-specific data\"; \"fine-tuned on task-specific data\"; \"final predictions and the true labels\"; \"transcription factor motifs\"; \"enhancer activity prediction\"; \"genomic benchmarks\"; \"biological questions\"; \"non-text, non-vision inputs\"; \"prediction of genomic features\"; \"DNA\"; \"pre-trained language models for genomics tasks\"; \"cross-modal fine-tuning\"; \"modalit[y] gap\"; \"domain-specific foundation models\"; \"genomic FMs\"; \"pre-training on DNA sequence data\"; \"figure 2\"; \"CNN embedder, transformer layers from a pre-trained language model\"; \"distribution distance between language embeddings and DNA embeddings\"; \"new method that incorporates a carefully designed architecture and improved alignment between different modalities\"; \"repurposing existing LLMs for genomics tasks\"; \"natural language processing (NLP)\"; \"cross-disciplinary applications of LLMs\"; \"transcription factor motifs\"; \"enhancer activity prediction\"; \"DNA embeddings and language embeddings\"; \"pre-trained language models\"; \"language models originally developed for NLP\"; \"genomic tasks\"; \"biological questions\"; \"task-specific loss\"; \"training in three stages\"; \"neural architecture search\"; \"superior performance to fine-tuned genomic FMs\"; \"domain-specific expert models\"; \"cross-modal transfer phenomenon\"; \"transformers pre-trained on natural language\"; \"general-purpose cross-modal fine-tuning method\"; \"bypass genomic pre-training altogether\"; \"a novel three-stage training procedure\"; \"simultaneously minimizes\"; \"distribution distance\"; \"language embeddings (h text) and DNA embeddings (h DNA)\"; \"cross-modal approaches\"; \"multiple genomics tasks\"; \"pre-trained language models\""},"architecture_reviewer":{"record_id":"full_2026-07-06__rec_000323","paper_type":"application_wrapper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The paper repurposes a pre-trained LLM for genomics via cross-modal fine-tuning and supervised task-specific training, rather than introducing a new generative model. It shows transferable, multi-task use across genomics benchmarks, but the candidate contribution is an application wrapper.","evidence_snippet":"\"transformer layers from a pre-trained language model\" and \"fine-tuned on task-specific data in a supervised manner\"; \"repurposing existing LLMs for genomics tasks\"; \"multiple genomics benchmarks\"; \"linear predictor\"\",\"evidence_for_text_component\":\"not_assessed\",\"evidence_for_text_bio_bridge\":\"not_assessed\",\"evidence_for_generative_model\":\"\"linear predictor\"; \"fine-tuned on task-specific data in a supervised manner\"\",\"boundary_case\":\"wrapper_boundary\"}]}}"},"python_gate":{"provisional_decision":"ADJUDICATE","provisional_code":"application_wrapper","adjudication_reason":"criterion_unclear_or_reviewer_conflict","paper_type":"primary