/Users/bogdan.didenko/lpnu/review/data/docling_uncertain_no_vlm_2026-07-08/chunks/full_2026_07_06_rec_003118.jsonl:28:{"candidate_id": "full_2026-07-06__rec_003118", "chunk_index": 28, "text": "313\n314\n315\n316\n317\n318\n319\n320\n321\n322\n323\noutput over the vocabulary and the ground truth one-hot label is computed for backpropagation (BP). However, only the universal LoRA and the LoRA for the current task are updated via gradient descent. This strategy aims to train a universal LoRA for domain transfer from general text to biomedical information, alongside a series of LoRAs specialized in SC analysis tasks. Moreover, the integration of LoRAs has demonstrated its superiority in zero-shot scenarios (Zhengmao et al., 2023).", "contextualized_text": "3 METHODOLOGY\n3.2 MULTI-MODAL MULTI-TASK INSTRUCTION TUNING WITH SINGLE-CELL DATA\n313\n314\n315\n316\n317\n318\n319\n320\n321\n322\n323\noutput over the vocabulary and the ground truth one-hot label is computed for backpropagation (BP). However, only the universal LoRA and the LoRA for the current task are updated via gradient descent. This strategy aims to train a universal LoRA for domain transfer from general text to biomedical information, alongside a series of LoRAs specialized in SC analysis tasks. Moreover, the integration of LoRAs has demonstrated its superiority in zero-shot scenarios (Zhengmao et al., 2023).", "headings": ["3 METHODOLOGY", "3.2 MULTI-MODAL MULTI-TASK INSTRUCTION TUNING WITH SINGLE-CELL DATA"], "pages": [6], "meta": {"schema_name": "docling_core.transforms.chunker.DocMeta", "version": "1.0.0", "doc_items": [{"self_ref": "#/texts/323", "parent": {"cref": "#/body"}, "children": [], "content_layer": "body", "meta": null, "label": "text", "prov": [{"page_no": 6, "bbox": {"l": 73.131, "t": 196.4844121999995, "r": 86.42512679999999, "b": 189.00048829999957, "coord_origin": "BOTTOMLEFT"}, "charspan": [0, 3]}]}, {"self_ref": "#/texts/324", "parent": {"cref": "#/body"}, "children": [], "content_lay