/Users/bogdan.didenko/lpnu/review/data/docling_uncertain_no_vlm_2026-07-08/chunks/full_2026_07_06_rec_003118.jsonl:94:{"candidate_id": "full_2026-07-06__rec_003118", "chunk_index": 94, "text": "849\n850\n851\n852\n853\n854\n855\n856\n857\n858\n859\n860\n861\n862\n863\nall non-zero values. Here, we set the number of bins as 10. So, for example, if a non-zero SC expression value is in the bottom 5% of all non-zero values, it's assigned to the 1st bin; if it is in the bottom 18%, it's assigned to the 2nd bin, and so on. ZerOmics does not focus on the specific SC expression value, but rather on its relative expression level. Therefore, in the pre-training stage of SC Model, all SC expression tokens include 12 types, namely 10 bin value tokens, zero value tokens, and the special mask token.", "contextualized_text": "A DATASETS INFORMATION\nA.3 DATA PREPROCESSING\n849\n850\n851\n852\n853\n854\n855\n856\n857\n858\n859\n860\n861\n862\n863\nall non-zero values. Here, we set the number of bins as 10. So, for example, if a non-zero SC expression value is in the bottom 5% of all non-zero values, it's assigned to the 1st bin; if it is in the bottom 18%, it's assigned to the 2nd bin, and so on. ZerOmics does not focus on the specific SC expression value, but rather on its relative expression level. Therefore, in the pre-training stage of SC Model, all SC expression tokens include 12 types, namely 10 bin value tokens, zero value tokens, and the special mask token.", "headings": ["A DATASETS INFORMATION", "A.3 DATA PREPROCESSING"], "pages": [16], "meta": {"schema_name": "docling_core.transforms.chunker.DocMeta", "version": "1.0.0", "doc_items": [{"self_ref": "#/texts/884", "parent": {"cref": "#/body"}, "children": [], "content_layer": "body", "meta": null, "label": "text", "prov": [{"page_no": 16, "bbox": {"l": 73.131, "t": 244.30541219999964, "r": 86.42512679999999, "b": 236.8214882999996, "coord_origin": "BOTTOMLEFT"}, "charspan": [0, 3]}]}, {"self_ref": "#/texts/885", "parent": 